---
/**
 * /pricing: THE canonical fee page. Every other property (homepage FAQ, blog
 * posts, docs, business, llms.txt) should state fees consistently with this
 * page and link here. Operated pricing is enforced by the Ophis backend;
 * hosted pricing uses the equivalent CIP-75 appData policy.
 *
 * FAQ answers are rendered VERBATIM as the visible section body (the postbuild
 * check-faq-schema gate requires schema text to appear in visible text), so
 * edit the FAQS constants, not the markup.
 */
import ContentPage from '../layouts/ContentPage.astro'
import { canonicalPage } from '../data/canonicalPages'

const { updated } = canonicalPage('/pricing/')

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'What does Ophis charge?',
    a: `Outside the current Arc release exception, the standard batch-auction schedule charges a 1 bp Ophis base. Ophis also retains 80% of reference-quote improvement on volatile pairs, capped at 99 bps of volume, or 50% on stable pairs, capped at 20 bps. CoW-hosted chains additionally pay CoW Protocol fees upstream.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the all-in cost on each chain?',
    a: `For standard-policy batch-auction swaps (not the current Arc exception), the minimum Ophis fee is 1 bp and the maximum Ophis charge is 100 bps on volatile pairs or 21 bps on stable pairs. On CoW-hosted chains, CoW Protocol adds its own fees on top.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Does Ophis take a cut of surplus?',
    a: `Under the standard policy, excluding Arc's current release exception: 80% on volatile pairs or 50% on stable pairs, subject to the caps. The measurement is improvement over the reference quote, not the user's slippage limit.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'What do integrators pay, and what can they charge?',
    a: `SDK v0.4.3 and hosted MCP integrations charge a 1 bp base on supported chains, including Arc. Other chains also apply the standard capped improvement policy; Arc currently has no backend improvement capture. Integrators can still charge an onboarded own-fee of up to 90 bps on top; Ophis's registered hosted configuration reserves a 190 bps aggregate ceiling. This is not a universal ceiling for every CoW widget or integration.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are the APIs free?',
    a: `Yes. The public Intent API and the MCP server are free to call. The Intent API is rate-limited to 30 requests per minute per IP; partner-tier rate limits are reviewed case by case.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'Are there rebates?',
    a: `On indexed chains, including Arc, volume rebate tiers (10% to 50% by rolling 30-day volume) weight your share of a monthly WETH rebate pool, and a referral layer pays 8% or 12% of the verified base fee Ophis keeps, monthly in WETH, on-chain. Eligibility requires verified settled trades. For Arc referrals, MCP clients pass referrerCode to build_order; direct SDK integrations use v0.4.4 or later.`,
  },
]
---

<ContentPage
  title="Ophis fees and pricing"
  description="Ophis fees: the standard base plus capped improvement policy, Arc's release exception, hosted upstream fees and bridge costs."
  path="/pricing/"
  heading="Fees and pricing"
  lede="Pricing by settlement path: standard batch-auction fees, the Arc release exception and route-specific bridge costs."
  updated={updated}
  faqs={FAQS}
>
  <p>
    <strong>The short version:</strong> the standard schedule, excluding the current Arc exception, charges 1 bp plus 80% of
    reference-quote improvement on volatile pairs (99 bps cap), or 50% on stable pairs (20 bps cap).
    CoW-hosted chains additionally pay CoW Protocol's upstream fees.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Path</th>
        <th scope="col">Optimism / Unichain / Robinhood</th>
        <th scope="col">CoW-hosted</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://swap.ophis.fi/">Swap app</a></td>
        <td>1 bp + 80% improvement (99 bps cap); 50%/20 bps cap for stables</td>
        <td>Same 1 bp + capped improvement policy</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://github.com/ophis-fi/ophis/tree/main/packages/sdk">@ophis/sdk</a> integrations</td>
        <td>Same sovereign model</td>
        <td>Same all-chain policy via CIP-75 appData</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/ai-agents">MCP server</a> (keyless)</td>
        <td>Same sovereign model</td>
        <td>Same all-chain policy via CIP-75 appData</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Intent API and MCP calls themselves</td>
        <td>Free</td>
        <td>Free</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  {FAQS.map((f) => (
    <section>
      <h2>{f.q}</h2>
      <p>{f.a}</p>
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Arc release exception</h2>
  <p>
    Arc is Ophis-operated but its running release currently configures no backend improvement
    policy. The verified completed USDC/EURC order carried a 1 bp volume-only fee. Do not assume
    the standard 80%/99 bps or 50%/20 bps capture applies there: review the quote and signed
    fee metadata. See the <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/fees#arc-release-exception">dated fee evidence</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Bridge costs and gas</h2>
  <p>
    These rates are not a total execution-cost estimate. Pool fees, price impact and wallet
    gas can affect net output. NEAR quotes include a 3 bps Ophis app fee and provider costs;
    direct Circle bridge and WBTC-conversion routes are separate from batch-auction pricing.
    Read <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/networks-assets">route restrictions and recovery rules</a>
    and review the final quote before authorizing a transfer.
  </p>

  <h2>Worked example</h2>
  <p>
    On $100,000 of Optimism volatile volume with 20 bps of improvement, Ophis receives $10 base
    plus $160 of improvement capture: $170 total. On a stable pair with the same improvement, the
    stable capture is 10 bps, producing $110 total; the 20 bps cap does not bind until improvement
    reaches 40 bps. Hosted chains apply the same Ophis base and improvement policy, with CoW
    Protocol's separate upstream fees added on top.
  </p>

  <h2>Sources and detail</h2>
  <p>
    Read <a href="/blog/solver-aligned-pricing/">why Ophis uses solver-aligned pricing</a>
    for the rationale behind the base fee and capped improvement capture.
  </p>
  <p>
    Chain-by-chain fee detail lives at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/fees">docs.ophis.fi/fees</a>,
    integrator terms at <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/partners">docs.ophis.fi/partners</a> and
    <a href="https://business.ophis.fi/">business.ophis.fi</a>, rebate mechanics at
    <a href="https://docs.ophis.fi/affiliate">docs.ophis.fi/affiliate</a>, and CoW Protocol's own
    fee schedule at <a href="https://docs.cow.fi/governance/fees">docs.cow.fi</a>. See also
    <a href="/supported-chains/">supported chains</a> for which chains are Ophis-operated.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
